At eleven in the morning, it was a bit quiet in the café.
Sunita ji called me over to her.
She said, "Maya, now we will learn to make bun maska."
There were many soft buns and butter kept on the table.
She picked up the first bun.
She taught me to cut the bun quickly.
She had applied a lot of butter inside the bun.
I watched her carefully.
Then I took the second bun.
I was learning to cut the bun quickly.
I cut it through the middle with a knife.
The bun was very soft.
I also applied butter generously on the bun.
It was a very fun task.
I was really enjoying doing this task.
Together, both of us had prepared many buns.
Sunita ji smiled and said, "Very good, Maya."
I had learned to do so much in just one morning.
